      "dom_id": "question-345539",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Find the average rate of change of the function $y=-2x$ over the interval $x\\in [4,4+h]$, where $h>0$ is a parameter.\n\nThe average rate of change is\n{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "Let $f(x)=-2x.$ Notice that we are given the length $h$ of the interval, so we use\n\n$$\n\\frac{Δy}{Δx}=\\frac{f(a+h)-f(a)}{h},\n$$\n\nwith $a=4.$ Substituting into the formula gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{Δy}{Δx} & =\\frac{f(4+h)-f(4)}{h} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2(4+h)-(-2)(4)}{h} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8-2h+8}{h} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2\\cancel{h}}{\\cancel{h}} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the average rate of change is $-2.$",
